  ('a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000007502', $m$codigo$m$, $m$SP5-840-006$m$, NULL, $m$Channel Max Sets the maximum number of channels available for data transmission via the wireless LAN. The number of channels available varies according to Service location. The default settings are set for the maximum end of the range for Program each area. Adjust the upper 4 bits to set the maximum number of channels. DFU Mode Tables Note: Do not change the setting. Europe/Asia: 1 to 13 NA/ Asia: 1 to 11 Channel Min Sets the minimum number of channels available for data transmission via the wireless LAN. The number of channels available varies according to location. The default settings are set for the minimum end of the range for$m$, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $m$[1 to 11 or 13 / 11 or 13 / 1 /step]$m$),
